# Text files have LF line endings in every checkout, Windows included,
# whatever core.autocrlf says: with CRLF, gofmt -l in make lint flags every
# Go file, and the files embedded with go:embed differ from machine to
# machine. Binary files, which git detects by their content (text=auto),
# are left as they are.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that go to the Linux server keep LF line endings in a Windows
# checkout too: with CRLF, bash and systemd choke on them.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.service  text eol=lf
